# social-skills — environment configuration.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values for the platforms you'll use.
# .env is git-ignored. Skills read it via grep|cut (NOT source) so passwords
# with shell-special chars ($, backtick, single-quote) are safe.
#
# Brand handles, company IDs, and topic filters live in config/brand.json
# (also gitignored). See PERSONAL.md.

# --- Instagram (per-account credentials) ---
# Convention: INSTAGRAM_<ACCOUNT_LABEL>_USERNAME / _PASSWORD.
# The account label is what you pass to /instagram-login <account> and is
# the suffix in ~/.config/agent-browser/instagram-<label>.json. The label
# should match brands.<slug>.instagram.default_account in brand.json.
#
# Example for an account label "myaccount":
#   INSTAGRAM_MYACCOUNT_USERNAME=
#   INSTAGRAM_MYACCOUNT_PASSWORD=

# --- LinkedIn (single account, no label split) ---
LINKEDIN_USERNAME=
LINKEDIN_PASSWORD=

# --- X / Twitter ---
# Username can be handle, email, or phone — X accepts any on the first screen.
# If you maintain multiple X accounts, sign in to all of them in the shared
# Chrome once; /x-post + /x-warm switch between them via the account switcher.
TWITTER_USERNAME=
TWITTER_PASSWORD=

# --- Pinterest ---
PINTEREST_USERNAME=
PINTEREST_PASSWORD=

# --- TikTok (manual login only) ---
# TikTok web sign-in has aggressive CAPTCHAs / slider puzzles even from real
# Chrome. Auto-login isn't worth attempting; sign in by hand once and the
# saved state at ~/.config/agent-browser/tiktok-default.json keeps you logged in.

# --- Browser identity ---
# Chrome profile dir — THE identifier for "our" Chrome. Cron guards use this
# to verify the agent-browser daemon is attached to OUR Chrome, not another
# project's. Set explicitly so cron + launch_browser.sh agree on the path.
SOCIAL_SKILLS_CHROME_PROFILE=~/.social-skills/chrome-profile
# SOCIAL_SKILLS_CHROME_BINARY=/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome

# --- iOS simulator (only if your composite skills drive an iOS app) ---
# Pin a specific simulator UDID for cron-fired skills. Leave empty to let the
# wrapper auto-select the first available iPhone 17.
SOCIAL_SKILLS_SIM_UDID=

# --- Claude Code subscription OAuth token (cron only) ---
# cron has no GUI session → can't unlock Keychain → claude can't read OAuth.
# Pull this from your `~/.zshrc` (the `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=` line).
# This is your subscription token (NOT an API key).
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# DO NOT add ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here — Claude Code (OAuth via your subscription)
# IS the agent. There is no API key in this stack.
